  "tolerance": "Every cents field within $1/year (100 cents) of the engine after documented rounding; tier labels exact.",
  "derivation": [
    "Household: one Single member born 1961-07-15 (age 65 in 2026; SECURE 2.0 RMD trigger age 75 for born 1960+, first RMD year 2036). On Medicare every projection year (whole-year model).",
    "Annual inputs, constant in nominal dollars: $80,000 pre-tax IRA withdrawal; $24,000 gross Social Security; $500,000 Dec-31 prior-year IRA balance (stylized flat-balance workbook assumption); no ACA coverage; no taxable-brokerage balance, no cash interest, no other income.",
    "inflationRatePct is omitted (zero-inflation model), so every year at or after 2026 resolves the 2026 statutory tables with a scaling factor of 1; the only year-varying statutory element is the senior deduction (expires after 2028) and the Table III divisor (age).",
    "SS taxation (26 USC 86, Single): provisional income = 80,000 + 0.5*24,000 = 92,000 > 34,000 -> 85% tier; taxable = min(0.85*24,000, 0.85*(92,000-34,000) + min(0.5*(34,000-25,000), 0.5*24,000)) = min(20,400, 49,300+4,500) = 20,400 every year.",
    "Ordinary income = 80,000 + 20,400 = 100,400; MAGI = 100,400 (no LTCG, no tax-exempt interest).",
    "Deductions: standard 16,100 + age-65 add-on 2,050 = 18,150. Senior deduction 2026-2028: 6,000 - 0.06*(100,400-75,000) = 4,476; 2029+: expired -> 0.",
    "Federal tax 2026-2028: taxable 77,774 -> 1,240 + 12%*(50,400-12,400) + 22%*(77,774-50,400) = 11,822.28. 2029+: taxable 82,250 -> 12,807.00. No LTCG tax; no NIIT (MAGI < 200,000).",
    "RMD (Pub 590-B Table III): 0 before age 75 (born 1960+ -> trigger 75); from 2036 RMD = 500,000 / divisor(age), rounded to cents (e.g. 2036 age 75: 500,000/24.6 = 20,325.20).",
    "IRMAA: lookback MAGI supplied only from 2028 (the two-year lookback ring is unpopulated for 2026-2027 -> engine skips IRMAA those years). Lookback MAGI $120,000 (stylized) > $109,000 and <= $137,000 -> individual tier 1: (81.20 + 14.50) * 12 = 1,148.40/yr for the single beneficiary."
  ],
